### Two milestones. The second exists so the cascade in 040 can delete one and leave the other's tasks
### standing — a cascade that took everything would look identical to one that took the right rows.
# @name CreateBeta
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/milestones
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{runToken}} Beta",
  "status": "active",
  "due_on": "2026-09-30"
}

###
# @name CreateLaunch
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/milestones
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{runToken}} Launch",
  "status": "planned",
  "due_on": "2026-12-01"
}

### Move Beta along, conditionally. `audit: true` is what mints the version the ETag is taken from.
# @name AdvanceBeta
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/milestones/{{CreateBeta.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}
If-Match: {{CreateBeta.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "done" }

### `status` is an enum with three declared values, and 'shipped' is not one of them
# @name NotADeclaredStatus
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/milestones
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{runToken}} Wrong", "status": "shipped" }

### The plan as it stands
# @name Plan
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/milestones?name=like.{{runToken}}%25&order=name.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{apiKeyId}}.{{apiKeySecret}}
